From: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hip: GraphNode::CaptureAndFormPacket must check the capture stream

hip::Device::NullStream() returns nullptr when the null stream cannot be
created (no HSA queue at the KFD memory limit). GraphNode::CaptureAndFormPacket
passed that pointer to CreateCommand, and amd::Command's constructor read the
queue through a null reference. Return hipErrorOutOfMemory instead, which is
what a failed stream creation reports elsewhere; hipGraphInstantiate then
returns the error and the application can report it. ROCm/clr develop has the
same unchecked call as of 2026-09-19.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
---
--- a/hipamd/src/hip_graph_internal.hpp
+++ b/hipamd/src/hip_graph_internal.hpp
@@ -251,6 +251,9 @@
                                   std::vector<uint8_t*>* batchPackets = nullptr,
                                   std::vector<std::string>* batchKernelNames = nullptr) {
     auto capture_stream = hip::getNullStream(g_devices[dev_id_]->devices()[0]->context(), false);
+    if (capture_stream == nullptr) {
+      return hipErrorOutOfMemory;
+    }
     hipError_t status = CreateCommand(capture_stream);
     if (status != hipSuccess) {
       return status;
